{"cuisine/cuisine-of-sao-tome-and-principe":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-sao-tome-and-principe","n":"Santomean cuisine","c":"#e46a3f","crumb":[["Africa","cuisines#africa"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of São Tomé and Principe","intro":[["Santomean cuisine comprises the cuisine, dishes and foods of São Tomé and Príncipe, a Portuguese-speaking island nation in the Gulf of Guinea, off the western equatorial coast of Central Africa. The country consists of two archipelagos around the two main islands: São Tomé and Príncipe, located about 140 kilometres (87 mi) apart and about 250 and 225 kilometres (155 and 140 mi), respectively, off the northwestern coast of Gabon."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-sao-tome-and-principe"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_São_Tomé_and_Príncipe"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]}],"cont":"African cuisine"},"cuisine/levantine-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/levantine-cuisine","n":"Levantine cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"Cuisine of a people","intro":[["Levantine cuisine is the traditional cuisine of the Levant. The cuisine has similarities with other Eastern Mediterranean cuisines, such as Balkan cuisine, particularly Greek Egyptian cuisine, North African cuisine, and Ottoman cuisine. It is particularly known for its meze spreads of hot and cold dishes, most notably among them Manakish pies, kibbeh, ful medames, hummus, tabbouleh and baba ghanoush, accompanied by bread."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"levantine-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levantine_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":3,"rows":[{"name":"The Levantine Vegetarian","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Salma Hage","note":"Meat-free recipes from across the Levant, published by Phaidon.","url